  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="af8319c9-4b6d-5671-ab59-42f10a31b9dd" activityNameId="91fb2243-48ee-5dc0-b701-a614a426ca05" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Plant offshore, natural gas, production</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Plant offshore, natural gas, production
Data relates to the platform Odin, which belonged to Esso Norway. The life time is 11 years with a total production of 27.7 Mrd. Nm3 natural gas.;
UUID: c2934807-7fb8-3b61-8bd0-f22e32198111
Material and energy requirements of a natural gas offshore platform.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Data relates to the platform Odin, which belonged to Esso Norway. The Odin platform is a gas installation with a steel jacket, on top drilling equipment, living quarters. It is fairly small (40x40x112 meters). The platform was installed in 1983 and the field closed in 1994. 1996 the platform was brought ashore for dismantling. 
Time period: Energy and water requirements out of 1980 data. The material requirements were reported in 1996.
Production volume: 27.7E9 Sm3 natural gas
Sampling: No information on sampling procedure. Standard transport distances are used. 
Extrapolations: The data for Odin are extrapolated for GLO. The total quantity of material is about 30% less as in Frischknecht et al. 1996. It is assumed that after dismantling ashore the materials are dumped in landfill. The energy and water requirements for construction and installation of the platform are assumed to be correlating to the weight of the equipment in the same relation as for the Leman field in Klitz 1980.
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_c2934807-7fb8-3b61-8bd0-f22e32198111.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="3320dcee-ac7b-51fa-8397-bc03eb397f03" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
